.TH delete n 2.0 Tclpp "Tclpp Built-In Commands"
.BS
.SH NAME
delete \- Delete an instance of a class
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdelete\fR \fIobject\fR 
.br
\fIobject\fR \fBdelete\fR 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete the object entirely (including all its contents) and invoke the
destructor of the object. The destructor of all its base classes and
of all its variables will be called as well.
.sp

Two methods are supported. The first is a command called \fBdelete\fR
and the other is calling an instance procedure called \fBdelete\fR. Both
are equivalent.
.SH AUTHOR(S)
Stefan Sinnige (ssinnige@geocities.com)
.SH SEE ALSO
class(n), new(n)
